Dear XFS folks,


[Linux: 4.14.x, and 4.19.x, xfsprogs: 4.19.0]

Over this weekend the problem below happened.

On a file server with NFS with Linux 4.14.x, due to probably an NFS
file handle leak, and a user script creating up to 600 files a second
(from five cluster jobs) the maximum number of allowed opened files
was reached (`/proc/sys/fs/file-max`), and everything hung.

    2019-02-16T09:58:49.540595+01:00 tinytina kernel: [1440251.572155] VF=
S: file-max limit 9847728 reached

As a work around we increased that limit dramatically, and everything els=
e
seemed to continue as planned.

    [1443503.169987] Process accounting resumed

A restart of the NFS daemon did not help, so to get rid of the leaked
file handles, the system was rebooted.

We moved to Linux 4.19 on other systems, so started that version here too=
,
but then found the messages below.

```
